1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,622
CHAPTER 6 — THE THIRTEEN-YEAR-OLD BOY

2
00:00:03,922 --> 00:00:12,450
In 2016, at the Venice Film Festival, Denis Villeneuve was asked what his dream project was. He answered: Dune.

3
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:17,611
A production company that had just bought the rights read the interview and called him.

4
00:00:17,791 --> 00:00:25,112
During pre-production, inside his father's old desk, they found the Dune storyboards he had drawn when he was 13.

5
00:00:25,292 --> 00:00:30,877
He filmed in the deserts of Jordan and Abu Dhabi, and split the novel into two movies.

6
00:00:31,057 --> 00:00:39,510
The pandemic delayed the release by nearly a year. The studio released it in theaters and on streaming the same day. Villeneuve protested.

7
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:48,537
Even so, it grossed over $400 million. And it won 6 Oscars, more than any other film that night.
